.TH WAYPARAM-GUI 1 "September 2026" "wayparam 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wayparam\-gui \- local web interface for wayparam
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wayparam\-gui
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wayparam\-gui
serves a small web interface for
.BR wayparam (1)
and streams results to the browser as they are found.
.PP
On startup it prints a URL containing a one\-time token to standard error and
opens it in a browser:
.PP
.RS
wayparam UI: http://127.0.0.1:8765/?t=<token>
.RE
.PP
The interface performs outbound requests to the Internet Archive on behalf of
whoever can reach it, so it is deliberately not reachable from the network. It
binds to the loopback interface only, requires the token on every request, and
rejects requests whose
.B Host
header is not the address it is listening on, which defends against DNS
rebinding. Binding to any other address is refused.
.PP
To use it from another machine, forward the port instead:
.PP
.RS
ssh \-L 8765:127.0.0.1:8765 user@host
.RE
.PP
Inside a strictly confined snap, open the printed URL yourself: a confined snap
cannot launch the host browser.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-host " " \fIADDRESS\fR
Bind address (default: 127.0.0.1). Only
.IR 127.0.0.1 ,
.I ::1
and
.I localhost
are accepted; anything else is refused with exit status 2.
.TP
.BR \-\-port " " \fIN\fR
Bind port (default: 8765). Use
.I 0
to let the system pick a free one; the port actually chosen appears in the
printed URL.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-browser
Do not try to open a browser. The URL is printed to standard error either way.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase log verbosity. Repeat for debug output.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The server was stopped normally.
.TP
.B 1
The address and port could not be listened on.
.TP
.B 2
A bind address outside the loopback interface was requested.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl\-C.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wayparam (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Alessandro Greco (aleff\-github)
